Spec: Example Application Behavior

Purpose:
  Translate the observable, mandatory application behavior from appsec-requirements-example.yaml into one SpecDD root specification while leaving implementation-only secure-coding guidance in the YAML catalog.

Must:
  # Category: Authentication & Access Control
  AC-003: The application MUST rate-limit every externally reachable API endpoint.
  AC-004: The application MUST authenticate end users through a central identity provider using OIDC or SAML and mandatory MFA.
  AC-006: The application MUST authorize access to each requested resource against the authenticated identity.
  # Category: Error Handling & Security Events
  EH-002: The application MUST return generic error messages to clients and retain detailed diagnostics only in server-side logs.
  # Category: Web & Frontend Security
  WEB-001: The application MUST protect session-authenticated state changes against cross-site request forgery and MUST NOT perform them through HTTP GET.

Scenario: repeated API requests are throttled
  Given a client is sending requests to an externally reachable API endpoint
  When the client exceeds the permitted request rate
  Then the application throttles further requests from that client

Scenario: end user starts a session
  Given an end user has no authenticated session
  When the user signs in
  Then the application authenticates the user through the central identity provider
  And the identity provider requires MFA

Scenario: user requests another user's resource
  Given an authenticated user does not own the requested resource and has no delegated access
  When the user requests that resource by its identifier
  Then the application denies access

Scenario: request processing fails unexpectedly
  When request processing raises an unexpected error
  Then the application returns a generic error response without internal details
  And the application records the detailed diagnostic server-side

Scenario: cross-site state-changing request
  Given a user has an authenticated browser session
  When another site submits a state-changing request without valid CSRF proof
  Then the application rejects the request
